$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 8-(3-Bromo-5-chloropyridin-4-yl)-2,8-diazaspiro[4.5]-decan-1-one 57 (35
mg, 0.10 mmol), tert-butyl
4-(4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)phenyl)piperazine-1-carboxylate
(39 mg, 0.10 mmol) and Pd(dppf)Cl2.CH2Cl2 (3.7 mg, 5.1 μmol) were loaded
in a microwave vial under argon and then MeCN (1.8 mL) and 0.5 M aqueous
sodium carbonate solution (284 μL, 0.142 mmol) were added. The reaction
mixture was heated under microwave irradiation at 120 °C for 60 min. The
solvent was concentrated and the crude material purified via Biotage
column chromatography (CH2Cl2/EtOH, 98.5:1.5 to 95:5).
Tert-butyl-4-(4-(5-chloro-4-(1-oxo-2,8-
diazaspiro[4.5]decan-8-yl)pyridin-3-yl)phenyl)piperazine-1-carboxylate
(43 mg, 80% yield) as a cream solid. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.30 –
1.37 (m, 2H), 1.49 (s, 9H), 1.94 – 2.00 (m, 4H), 2.69 – 2.79 (m, 2H),
3.09 – 3.15 (m, 2H), 3.19 – 3.23 (m, 4H), 3.29 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 3.58
– 3.63 (m, 4H), 6.19 (bs, 1H), 6.99 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 7.19 (d, J = 8.7
Hz, 2H), 8.17 (s, 1H), 8.39 (s, 1H); LC (Method C)- MS (ESI, m/z) Rt =
2.89 min – 526/528 (M+H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, microwave irradiation, thermal, microwave vial used,
Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Potent, Orally Bioavailable, Small-Molecule Inhibitors of
WNT Signaling from a Cell-Based Pathway Screen
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mallinger, Aurelie; Crumpler, Simon; Pichowicz, Mark; Waalboer, Dennis;
Stubbs, Mark; Adeniji-Popoola, Olajumoke; Wood, Bozena; Smith, Elizabeth;
