$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the synthesis of
Pyridone Ik and Il Pyridone of general structure D (0.49 mmol),
Benzo[b]thien-3-ylboronic acid (0.99mmol), Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (0.024 mmol), and
KF (0.99 mmol) were dissolved in MeOH (4.0 mL), and the reaction heated
by MWI at 140 °C for 10 min. The reaction mixture was diluted with
CH2Cl2. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4,
filtered, and concentrated. Purification by column chromatography eluting
with (Heptane:ethyl acetate 1:1→1:9) gave desired compound. Methyl
(3R)-4-oxo-6-{(7-thiabicyclo[4.3.0]nona-1,3,5,8-tetraen-9-yl)methyl}-7-[m-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]-1-thia-3a-aza-3-indancarboxylate(Il):
Prepared by following the general procedure, white foam, 320mg (73%).
[α]D-147 (c 1.0, CHCl3); IR ν 1750, 1652, 1577, 1484, 1348, 1211, 713
cm-1; 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) 3.46 (dd, J = 1.2, 12.0 Hz, 1H), 3.68 (dd,
J = 8.8, 11.2 Hz, 1H), 3.71 (s, 2H), 3.84 (s, 3H), 5.66 (dd, J = 2.4, 8.8
Hz, 1H), 6.23 (s, 1H), 6.89 (s, 1H), 7.23-7.45 (m, 6H), 7.53 (d, J =7.6
Hz, 1H), 7.80 (dd, J = 0.8, 8.0Hz, 1H); 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 31.9,
32.8, 53.5, 63.6, 114.6, 115.7, 121.4, 122.9, 124.1, 124.4(2C), 125.2,
129.4, 131.8, 133.3, 133.6, 136.9, 138.1, 140.3, 147.5, 152.7, 161.2,
168.4. LCMS m/z = 502 (M+H), C25H18F3NO3S2 requires 501.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Multiring Fused 2-Pyridones via a Nitrene Insertion
Reaction: Fluorescent Modulators of α-Synuclein Amyloid Formation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
